# WebDAVHandler @VERSION@ - WebDAV and Nextcloud servers as a volume

webdav-handler is a filesystem handler for AmigaOS 4. The volume
`WebDAV:` (device `WDV:`) shows every server you add with the prefs
program wdvprefs as a drawer, for example `WebDAV:Home`. Inside it are
the files on the server: Workbench, the Shell and every program can open,
copy, rename, delete and save them as on any other disk. Nextcloud,
ownCloud, NAS boxes, hosting services and web servers such as Apache
work; on Nextcloud the handler also keeps file dates and uploads big
files in parts.

**Beta testers wanted.** webdav-handler is new and has been tested with
Nextcloud and Apache in an emulated AmigaOne only. Please try it with
your own servers and on real hardware, and report what does not work
(which server, what you did, what happened; the guide explains how to
get a debug log). Bug reports are welcome as comments on this OS4Depot
page.

webdav-handler is an [OpenAmiga.org project](http://openamiga.org/?function=gitproject&name=webdav-handler).
The source code, test versions and bug reports are at
<https://github.com/OpenAmiga-org/webdav-handler>.

## Features

- Any number of servers in one device, set up with the prefs program
  wdvprefs ("Test connection" button included). Each server's type is
  found by itself (Nextcloud or plain WebDAV) or can be set.
- A server is connected when its drawer is first opened, and connected
  again by itself after network problems, so `WDV:` can be mounted at
  boot.
- Encrypted connections (https) through AmiSSL, with certificate check;
  a server's own certificate can be given.
- Files of any size; on Nextcloud big files are uploaded in parts, so
  server limits on request size do not matter.
- Names with national characters (UTF-8 on the server), upper and lower
  case ignored as on any Amiga volume.
- Comments (`FileNote`) are kept on the server; on Nextcloud also file
  dates (`Copy CLONE`, `SetDate`).
- Passwords can be saved with the server, or asked for with a requester.
- A failed upload is reported with a requester, and the data is kept
  locally, so nothing is lost.
- AmigaOS 4.1 style icons, with a volume icon for `WDV:`.

## Requirements

Not included, get them from OS4Depot:

- clib4.library 2.5 or newer: `development/library/misc/clib4.lha`
- AmiSSL 5 (5.1 or newer) or AmiSSL 6: `library/misc/amissl.lha`
- filesysbox.library 54.8 or newer (AmigaOS 4.1 Final Edition updates)

Tested with AmigaOS 4.1 Final Edition Update 3 and its Roadshow TCP/IP
stack. When AmiSSL 5 and 6 are both installed, AmiSSL 6 is used.

## Installation

Double-click `Install`. It checks the requirements, copies the handler to
`L:` and wdvprefs to `SYS:Prefs`, installs the DOSDriver `WDV` and the
volume icon, mounts `WDV:` and starts wdvprefs so that you can add your
servers. `WebDAVHandler.guide` has all the details.

webdav-handler was called Nextcloud Handler up to version 0.39. The
Install script offers to remove it, and wdvprefs takes its servers over
(the server list of 0.38/0.39 and the DOSDrivers of 0.37 and older).

## Using it

The servers are kept with the prefs program wdvprefs (name, address,
type, user, password, certificate). Its "Test connection" button tries
the settings before you save them. The top level of `WDV:` only lists the
servers: it does not connect and cannot be changed. For Nextcloud, use an
app password (Settings, Security in the Nextcloud web page).

## License

webdav-handler is public domain. It contains libcurl (curl licence),
Expat (MIT licence), zlib (zlib licence) and parts of clib4 (BSD
licence); see `Third-party.txt`.

## History

### 0.43 (18.11.2026)

- Clearer messages for some server answers: "file is write protected"
  for changes the server does not allow (read-only shares), "object is in
  use" for locked files, "disk is full" for files too big for the server
  (they showed "Error -1").

### 0.42 (17.11.2026)

- Works with AmiSSL 6 alone and with every AmiSSL 5 from 5.1 on (before,
  it needed AmiSSL 5.27). wdvprefs' Test connection names the AmiSSL
  used.

### 0.41 (17.11.2026)

- Nextcloud Handler is now WebDAV Handler (`webdav-handler`, device
  `WDV:`, volume `WebDAV:`, prefs program wdvprefs); any WebDAV server
  works and Nextcloud servers keep their extras.
- A Type for every server (Automatic, Nextcloud, WebDAV).
- Install removes Nextcloud Handler on request and wdvprefs takes its
  servers over.
- AmigaOS 4.1 style icons and a volume icon for `WDV:`.
- Setting a date on a server that cannot keep it is accepted without
  effect. Reading files with a weak ETag works.
- With clib4.library older than 2.5 the handler shows a requester instead
  of stopping the boot.

### 0.39 (17.11.2026)

- Nextcloud Handler: one device, `NCH:`, for all servers: every server is
  a drawer, connected when it is first used. The new prefs program
  nchprefs keeps the server list (with "Test connection") and takes over
  the servers of the old DOSDrivers.
- Remembered passwords go into the server list. The character set of file
  names comes from `ENV:Charset` when CHARSET is not given. Long server
  messages are broken into lines in requesters.

### 0.37 (15.11.2026)

- Nextcloud Handler: converting an empty text between the Amiga character
  set and UTF-8 could give leftover memory instead of an empty text (no
  case is known where the handler showed it).

### 0.32 (15.11.2026)

- Nextcloud Handler: reading stops with an error when the file is changed
  on the server during the read, instead of giving a mix of both versions.
- The handler's code is freed when the volume is dismounted (about 3 MB
  were lost with every mount). Problems that need the user, such as
  certificate errors, are shown in a requester once.
- Names with ":" from the server can be used (shown as `%u003A`). Files
  show the e bit, so programs on the volume can be started. Line breaks in
  requesters are shown correctly. Files over 2 GiB can be written with
  TEMPDIR on an FFS partition.

### 0.25 (15.11.2026)

- Nextcloud Handler: first test version.
